{
  "title": "Configuration version 2 → version 3",
  "description": "Where every key of a version 2 configuration (docs/configuration.md) goes in version 3, for ConfigMigration.upgrade (Domain/Config) and the importer (plan §29, phase 5). Version 1 files are first upgraded to version 2 as today (templates still at the v1 defaults get the v2 defaults). 'from' paths are relative to the v2 type named before the colon; 'to' paths to the v3 schema definition named before the colon (Config = the document root). tools/check-contracts.py checks that every key of shared/fixtures/config/config2-everything.json has an entry and that every 'to' path exists in config-3.json. The golden results are in shared/fixtures/config/config-migration-cases.json.",
  "rules": [
    "Every v2 drive configuration (defaultDrive, drives[], presets[].config) becomes a profile. Profiles whose contents are identical (ignoring id and name) are merged into one; the first one's id is kept.",
    "defaultDrive becomes the profile with id 'default' (name kept) and its automation becomes automation.defaults. It gets no drives[] entry.",
    "drives[i] becomes a drives[] entry with the same id (lower-cased), name, enabled and match, the automation, the settings as makemkvSettings, and profile = its profile's id. Its profile is named after the drive and has id 'profile-<drive id>' unless it was merged into another.",
    "presets[i] becomes a profile with the preset's id and name; the preset's automation and match are dropped (a profile has neither).",
    "A profile keeps only the values that differ from what it inherits: the v3 defaults overlaid with the default profile (for the default profile, the v3 defaults alone). A drive's automation is omitted (null) when it equals automation.defaults; otherwise it is written in full.",
    "A step of a drive's postProcess with no matchName and no matchFormats goes into its profile's steps. One with either becomes a rule {when: {nameOrLabel, formats, profiles: [that profile]}, then: {steps: [id]}}.",
    "Every plugin becomes a step and a rule {when: {nameOrLabel, formats}, then: {steps: [id]}} in plugin order; an empty when matches every disc. Profile steps run before rule steps, as drive steps ran before plugins.",
    "outputRoot becomes the library 'library' (name = the folder's name); each distinct non-empty rootOverride another library 'library-2', 'library-3', … and the profile's library. The importer writes the markers only after the owner confirms (I2).",
    "Secrets leave the document: their values are returned next to the configuration and stored with ConfigService.setSecret. The fields get SecretRefs.",
    "Ids are lower-cased. Values a v3 field doesn't accept (an audioCD mode in rip.mode, say) become the default and produce the issue config.migration.valueDropped.",
    "Entries without an id get one from their place: 'drive-1', 'drive-2', … for drives, 'step-1', … for steps (drive steps, then plugins, in order), so the result is the same on every platform. Rules get 'rule-<step id>'.",
    "Unknown keys are dropped with the warning config.unknownKey (its path in the v2 document)."
  ],
